{
 "id": "2026-11-23-ai-agents-zero-day",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "AI agents hacked a university server through an unknown flaw. Who sent them?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Amazon's security team says attackers ran AI agents on Cairn, an open-source hacking toolkit. Their target: MONAI Label, software researchers use to label medical images. In about eleven minutes, Amazon says, the agents went from mapping it to writing files on the server."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "The bug let a crafted file name drop uploads anywhere on the machine. Its developers rate it critical, and say login is off by default. But on another university server, the agents tried for sixteen hours and a hundred and forty-eight steps, and failed."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Amazon links the campaign to a China-linked group, with moderate confidence, citing Chinese-language prompts and China time settings. Its security chief, CJ Moses, says defenders should let automated systems act on clear alerts, without waiting for a human."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will AI agents soon find most new software flaws? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
