 "upload": {
  "title": "Amazon: AI Agents Found and Used an Unknown Flaw #shorts",
  "description": "Amazon Threat Intelligence said on November 20, 2026 that attackers ran autonomous AI agents on the open-source Cairn framework and exploited a previously unknown path-traversal flaw in MONAI Label, open-source software for labelling medical images, going from mapping it to writing files on a university server in about 11 minutes. Against another university server the agents tried for about 16 hours and 148 steps without success. Amazon attributes the campaign to a China-linked actor with moderate confidence. MONAI Label's developers rate the flaw critical in their November 18 advisory (versions 0.8.5 and earlier; authentication off by default).\n\nSources: Amazon Threat Intelligence (via coverage), MONAI Label security advisory GHSA-qc22-rmgc-vg94 (GitHub), SecurityWeek, The Register, Technology.org, Startup Fortune, Gridinsoft.\n\n#tech #AI #cybersecurity #AIagents #Amazon #zeroday",
